{#
  Listed in manifests_files only while navidrome has pods, because a route to a workload with
  no pods is not free. Traefik's kubernetescrd provider re-reads every IngressRoute on each
  config refresh and logs `error ... no servers found for homelab/navidrome` whenever the
  EndpointSlice behind one is empty — every ~20s, forever, while navidrome sits at replicas 0.
  That drowns the traefik log, which is where a real edge failure shows up first (#1323).

  The gate lives in tasks/main.yml rather than here. The role arms `manifests_prune`, whose
  labelling wrapper refuses a template that renders no document, and dropping the name from
  the list is what makes the prune delete the live route.
#}
---
{{ ingressroute(
    container_item.name,
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
    container_item.use_authelia,
  )
}}
